# MinimalShop — Project Rules

## What this repo is
Next.js storefront (MinimalShop) that consumes the Minimal Ecommerce API under /api/v1.
Editorial "paper and ink" design with a single glass layer. Buyer, seller and superadmin roles.

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router) + React + TypeScript (strict mode). No JavaScript files.
- Styling: CSS Modules, one file per component, plus tokens in styles/tokens.css.
- Motion: Motion (motion.dev) for component-level animation; GSAP + ScrollTrigger for
  sequences and scroll. Never both on the same element.
- Icons: Lucide. Fonts: next/font (Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, Newsreader, IBM Plex Mono).
- Data: one typed HTTP client in lib/api/. DTO types mirror the API contracts exactly.

## Structure
- app/                routes, layouts, server components
- components/ui/      design system primitives (Button, Field, Dialog, GlassSurface...)
- components/features/ feature-specific composition
- styles/tokens.css   every design token as a CSS custom property
- lib/api/            client, endpoints, error mapping
- lib/motion/         shared variants, easings and GSAP helpers

## Commands
- pnpm dev            local dev server
- pnpm build          production build (must pass with zero warnings)
- pnpm lint           ESLint, zero errors
- pnpm typecheck      tsc --noEmit
- pnpm test           unit tests

## Non-negotiable rules
1. Read DESIGN.md before writing any UI. It is the contract, not a suggestion.
2. Never hardcode a color, space, radius, shadow or duration. Use tokens from styles/tokens.css.
3. Glass (`--glass-*`) only on floating surfaces: nav, dialog, sheet, toast, chip, price tag.
   Never on content blocks, never glass on glass, max two per screen.
4. Do not invent components that are not in DESIGN.md. If one is missing, propose it first.
5. Accessibility is a gate: WCAG 2.2 AA, visible focus, keyboard complete, `aria-live` for
   dynamic updates, 44px touch targets, `prefers-reduced-motion` and `prefers-reduced-transparency`
   honored.
6. All network access goes through lib/api/. No fetch calls inside components.
7. TypeScript strict: no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no non-null assertion to silence errors.
8. Never commit secrets. Every key lives in .env.local and is git-ignored.

## API rules
- Base URL from NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL. All paths under /api/v1.
- Auth: JWT access token plus rotating refresh. Send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- Forward `x-correlation-id` from the API response into logs; never strip it.
- Map API errors to a typed union in lib/api/errors.ts; never surface a raw message.
- Pagination is mandatory on list endpoints; page size never above the API limit (50).
- See docs/API.md for the resource map and docs/CAPABILITIES.md for module flags.

## Style of code
- One component per file, named export matching the file.
- Props interface: `<ComponentName>Props`.
- Server components by default; add `'use client'` only when state, effects or motion need it.
- Animations live in lib/motion/ as reusable helpers. No ad-hoc timings per component.
- Tests colocated as `<component>.test.tsx`.

## Verification before finishing
1. `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` clean.
2. `pnpm test` green; visual check at 360, 768 and 1024.
3. No hardcoded values (grep the diff for `#` and for `px` outside tokens).
4. Keyboard and axe pass; reduced-motion pass shows a static version.
5. Screenshot compared against the Figma frame.

## Never
- Never install a UI library, icon set or animation library without approval.
- Never use Tailwind, styled-components or a CSS-in-JS runtime.
- Never use Inter, Roboto, Arial or Space Grotesk.
- Never add dark mode, infinite scroll or a full-screen spinner.
- Never break the contract: the frontend adapts to the API DTOs, not the other way around.